// ⚠⚠ THE **EMITTING** CONFIG — what `npm run build` runs, and therefore what Firebase
// deploys. It sees `src` ONLY.
//
// ⚠ DO NOT ADD `test` HERE. See the note in `tsconfig.json`: with `test` in the input
// set the root dir moves up a level, `lib/index.js` becomes `lib/src/index.js` and the
// deployed bundle loses its entry point while gaining 124 compiled test files.
//
// ⚠ `rootDir: "src"` IS EXPLICIT, so the emit layout is fixed by this file rather than
// inferred from whatever happens to be in `include`.
//
// Mirrors `packages/game-server/tsconfig.build.json` and stage-engine's.
//
// ⚠ ONE DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM THOSE TWO: `npm run build` here runs
// `tsc --noEmit && tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` — the typecheck pass FIRST, then the
// emit. game-server and stage-engine keep `build` and `typecheck` separate.
//
// The reason is `firebase.json`, whose functions predeploy hook runs
// `npm --prefix functions run build`. Chaining puts `test/` inside the DEPLOY GATE
// rather than in a script somebody has to remember. A gate nothing invokes
// automatically is how this gap opened in the first place: `test/` was uncompiled for
// the whole life of the game and a fixture went silently vacuous inside it.
// Measured cost: 1.9s on top of a 1.7s emit.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "lib"
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
